       "quote": "Assume AC. Let $\\mu_0,\\mu_1\\in\\mathcal P_2(\\mathbb R^d)$. A generalized $W_2$ geodesic from $\\mu_0$ to $\\mu_1$ with base $\\nu\\in\\mathcal P_2(\\mathbb R^d)$ is a probability measure $\\pi$ on triples $(z,x,y)$ whose $(z,x)$ marginal is an optimal coupling of $\\nu$ and $\\mu_0$ and whose $(z,y)$ marginal is an optimal coupling of $\\nu$ and $\\mu_1$; its interpolating curve is $\\mu_t=((1-t)x+ty)_\\#\\pi$. A functional $F$ is $\\lambda$-convex along generalized geodesics if for every such $\\pi$ its values satisfy $F(\\mu_t)\\le(1-t)F(\\mu_0)+tF(\\mu_1)-\\frac{\\lambda}{2}t(1-t)\\int|x-y|^2d\\pi$. A vector field $g_\\mu\\in L^2(\\mu;\\mathbb R^d)$ is a strong Wasserstein subgradient of $F$ at $\\mu$ if for every $\\eta\\in\\mathcal P_2(\\mathbb R^d)$ and every coupling $\\gamma$ of $\\mu$ and $\\eta$, $F(\\eta)\\ge F(\\mu)+\\int g_\\mu(x)\\cdot(y-x)d\\gamma+o\\!\\left((\\int|y-x|^2d\\gamma)^{1/2}\\right)$ as the coupling action tends to zero, with a remainder uniform over all such couplings. The definition imposes no global displacement-convexity claim.",
